// Nuclear Thermal Rocket Engine Definitions
// NTR engines heat hydrogen propellant through a solid-core fission reactor.
// ~2x the Isp of chemical Hydrolox, moderate thrust. No external power needed.
// New propellant type: Hydrogen (pure LH2, no oxidizer)

